# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: ec-09-undertow
number: 309
name: Undertow
pool: Ordinary
description: Corner a Lobber and it retreats north up a pit column, straight into a Grappler's band. Chasing the ranged unit is the trap; the pull is only the invoice.
retired: superseded by ec-09-undertow-v2, which carries the same thesis over connected blocking mass and a question still live on round 3 (D-280). Kept parseable: the replay logs of every run that played it still name this id.
design: Enemy composition 9 — the Lobbers run backwards on purpose, and something is waiting back there.

spawn g = Grappler
spawn l = Lobber
spawn h = Husk

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ...g..B
  .^O.O^B
  ......B
  ..l.l..
  .H...H.
  A......
  AA..h..
